North Korea is issuing a new threat of  military action against the US the state  news agency says Americans should expect  to face an unimaginable strike at an  unexpected time the warning comes just  two days after a North Korean official  said a nuclear war may break out at any  moment  then Tracie is in Beijing with how the  provocative statements may be a response  to naval exercises nearby van good  morning  good morning in this latest threat North  Korea also calls the u.s. and South  Korea war mongers who may start a  nuclear war now this latest threat comes  at a time which appears to be a lull in  North Korea's missile tests the country  has not launched one in more than a  month but North Korea does appear to be  clearly upset about joint military  exercises that the u.s. and South Korea  navies are currently conducting in  waters off the Korean Peninsula this  includes the USS Ronald Reagan aircraft  carrier as well as Navy destroyers now  the US military says these war games are  designed to increase the readiness of  u.s. and South Korean forces but North  Korea sees them as a rehearsal for an  invasion the North says these military  exercises are driving the tension into  the worst line of explosion and prove  the u.s. and South Korea are attempting  to ignite a war on the Korean Peninsula  now the military exercises do end on  Friday but next week the US military is  planning to hold a rehearsal for how  they would evacuate US citizens from  South Korea if a war did break out Jeff  Ben Tracy thank you very much
 

